  <p class="positioning">ZxBudget is a privacy-focused zero-based budgeting app — a native app for iPhone, iPad, and Mac.</p>

  <div class="features">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Private, on or offline</h2>
      <p>Your budgets stay in your private iCloud. We never see the transactions. They keep working with no connection until your devices catch up.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Home shows the next step</h2>
      <p>Spending pace, what is left to assign, then the checklist: assign, targets, approve, and reconcile.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Add a transaction</h2>
      <p>The payee and category are suggested from where you are and what you usually buy, and you can scan a receipt on the device.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Registered accounts</h2>
      <p>Track your RRSP (including Spousal RRSP), TFSA, and RESP contribution room.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label">Also included</p>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li><strong>Credit cards stay covered</strong> Spending on a card sets the payment aside in that card’s category, so the money is waiting when the bill is due.</li>
    <li><strong>Assign the month in one tap</strong> One tap fills the month’s categories based on targets you set.</li>
    <li><strong>Foreign transactions</strong> Foreign accounts convert at public rates, and so does a purchase you enter in another currency on a credit card.</li>
    <li><strong>Share a budget</strong> Share your budget with another iCloud user.</li>
    <li><strong>Family Sharing</strong> One person pays for up to 6 people in your Apple Family Sharing group, and each person keeps their own iCloud account.</li>
    <li><strong>Upcoming transactions</strong> Schedule pay, rent, and bills, and see whether this month can cover them.</li>
    <li><strong>Reimbursements</strong> Mark a purchase Reimbursable, see who owes you under Awaiting reimbursement, and Apply what is still owed.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports</strong> Spending by category, income versus spending, reimbursements, net worth, sustainable spending, and milestones, plus registered-account room, and a currency view when you have foreign accounts.</li>
    <li><strong>Tracking accounts</strong> A house, a car, or investments that sit outside the spending accounts, so net worth includes what you own.</li>
  </ul>

